In the present case, alleged occurrence took place on 14.09.2021 and an application under Section 156(3) Cr.P.C. was filed on 26.11.2021 i.e. after more than two and a half months.
It has been alleged that applicant was a friend of husband of victim and he has friendly entrance in her house and took advantage of friendship and raped her, however, even then husband of victim has not taken any steps to lodge an F.I.R.
In these circumstances, delay of two and a half month become crucial, though victim has supported the case of prosecution in statement recorded under Section 164 Cr.P.C., however, considering age of victim as well as nature of allegation that there is a substantial delay in approaching Magistrate as well as taking note that applicant is in jail since 30.08.2022, a case of bail is made out, however,
learned trial court is directed to take all endeavour to record statement of victim within a period of 12 weeks.
